course: dictionary
lesson: 3743
title: Flow: the word that moves
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flow is a verb and a noun. As a verb, it means to move along smoothly and steadily in one direction. Water flows downhill because of gravity. «Electricity only flows when it has a complete loop to go round.» Here flows tells you that electricity keeps moving round the loop, like water in a river.
explain: Flow can also be a noun, meaning a steady movement of something. «Electricity is a flow of tiny charged particles through a material.» So a flow is the steady movement itself, just as the flow of a river is the water moving along it.
explain: Flow is not only about water. People, traffic and ideas can flow too. «The traffic flowed smoothly» means the cars moved steadily, with no jams. Hair or clothes can flow as well, hanging down loosely.
explain: When you meet flow in a new text, look at the clues. Is it a liquid, a gas, electricity, people or words? If the sentence describes steady, smooth movement, flow probably means that. Swap in move smoothly and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Flow means to move along smoothly and steadily in one direction.
fact: Liquids flow, but solids do not: they keep their own shape.
fact: Water flows downhill because of gravity, and rivers flow to the sea.
fact: «Electricity flows only around a complete circuit.»
fact: Fast-flowing rivers are dangerous, so never swim in them.
exercise: «Electricity only flows when it has a complete loop to go round.» What does flows mean here? | Sits still in the bulb | Gets hotter and hotter | *Moves steadily along a path | Stops and waits
exercise: Which of these does NOT flow? | *A wooden table | Water | Air | Lava
exercise: «The traffic flowed smoothly.» What does flowed mean? | Went backwards at great speed | Shouted loudly | Stopped in a big jam | *Moved steadily with no jams
test: Which word in «Electricity is a flow of tiny charged particles» is a noun meaning a steady movement? | particles | *flow | charged | Electricity
test: Why are fast-flowing rivers dangerous? | *Because the fast water can pull you along and you could drown | Because the water is cold | Because they are shallow | Because they have no fish
exam: Which sentence uses flow as a noun? | *«There is a steady flow of air through the open window.» | «Hair flows down her back.» | «Wind and sunshine keep flowing.» | «The water flowed down the hill.»
